1
00:00:00,700 --> 00:00:03,039
Welcome to this Talentora tutorial.

2
00:00:03,239 --> 00:00:08,332
In the next few minutes, you'll learn how to
build a complete job board on WordPress,

3
00:00:08,332 --> 00:00:11,508
from posting your first job to managing
applications.

4
00:00:12,488 --> 00:00:16,043
Talentora is a free job board plugin for
WordPress.

5
00:00:16,243 --> 00:00:20,219
To get started, install and activate it from
the plugin directory,

6
00:00:20,219 --> 00:00:21,845
just like any other plugin.

7
00:00:22,525 --> 00:00:27,189
Once it's active, a new Talentora menu appears
in your WordPress dashboard.

8
00:00:27,389 --> 00:00:32,757
From here you can manage jobs, categories, job
types, applications and settings.

9
00:00:32,957 --> 00:00:35,360
To post a job, click Add New Job.

10
00:00:36,040 --> 00:00:39,104
On the new job screen, start with the job
title.

11
00:00:39,304 --> 00:00:42,304
For example, Senior WordPress Plugin
Developer.

12
00:00:42,984 --> 00:00:45,429
Then write the job description in the editor.

13
00:00:45,629 --> 00:00:47,883
I'm using sample text for this demo.

14
00:00:48,563 --> 00:00:50,880
Next comes the Job Details box.

15
00:00:51,080 --> 00:00:53,263
Enter the location, the salary range,

16
00:00:53,263 --> 00:00:56,214
the experience level, and the number of
vacancies.

17
00:00:56,414 --> 00:00:58,944
Then add the working hours and working days.

18
00:00:59,624 --> 00:01:04,352
Pick the application deadline and the expected
joining date from the date picker.

19
00:01:04,552 --> 00:01:07,224
You can also set an optional expiry date,

20
00:01:07,224 --> 00:01:10,091
after which the job is hidden automatically.

21
00:01:10,771 --> 00:01:14,198
In Company Information, add the company name
and website.

22
00:01:14,878 --> 00:01:18,949
Then click Upload Logo, and pick an image from
your media library,

23
00:01:18,949 --> 00:01:20,182
or upload a new one.

24
00:01:20,862 --> 00:01:24,267
Under Application Settings, choose how
candidates apply.

25
00:01:24,467 --> 00:01:28,661
Use the built-in application form, or connect
a third-party form,

26
00:01:28,661 --> 00:01:31,435
such as Contact Form 7, with its shortcode.

27
00:01:31,635 --> 00:01:35,163
The Job Status toggle lets you mark a job as
filled,

28
00:01:35,163 --> 00:01:37,537
so it stops accepting applications.

29
00:01:38,217 --> 00:01:41,644
In the sidebar, choose a job category and a
job type.

30
00:01:41,844 --> 00:01:44,481
You can even create a new category right here.

31
00:01:45,161 --> 00:01:47,436
When everything looks good, click Publish.

32
00:01:48,116 --> 00:01:50,492
And here's your job, live on the site,

33
00:01:50,492 --> 00:01:54,743
with the salary, deadline, company details,
and an Apply Now button.

34
00:01:55,423 --> 00:02:00,066
To list your jobs anywhere on your site, use
the [talentora_jobs] shortcode.

35
00:02:00,746 --> 00:02:03,917
Add it to any page with a Shortcode block, and
publish.

36
00:02:04,117 --> 00:02:08,589
Visitors will see your job listings, with a
search and filter bar on top.

37
00:02:09,269 --> 00:02:11,277
The search form works with Ajax,

38
00:02:11,277 --> 00:02:15,042
so visitors can narrow down jobs without
reloading the page.

39
00:02:15,722 --> 00:02:17,783
Click View Details to open a job.

40
00:02:17,983 --> 00:02:21,808
Further down, candidates find the built-in
application form,

41
00:02:21,808 --> 00:02:25,506
with name, email, phone, resume upload and a
cover letter.

42
00:02:26,186 --> 00:02:29,546
To test this, I'm using a temporary email
address,

43
00:02:29,546 --> 00:02:32,301
so we can see the emails Talentora sends.

44
00:02:32,981 --> 00:02:38,321
Fill in the name, email and phone number,
attach a resume as a PDF or Word file,

45
00:02:38,321 --> 00:02:42,125
write a short cover letter, and click Submit
Application.

46
00:02:42,805 --> 00:02:46,125
The candidate immediately sees a confirmation
message.

47
00:02:46,805 --> 00:02:51,128
A confirmation email lands in the candidate's
inbox right away.

48
00:02:51,808 --> 00:02:56,835
You can customize every email under Talentora,
Settings, Email Templates.

49
00:02:57,035 --> 00:03:00,744
Edit the subject and message for the admin
notification,

50
00:03:00,744 --> 00:03:04,851
the applicant confirmation, and the status
change email, using

51
00:03:04,851 --> 00:03:08,163
placeholders such as applicant name and job
title.

52
00:03:08,843 --> 00:03:12,398
Every submission appears under Talentora,
Applications.

53
00:03:12,598 --> 00:03:17,816
You can filter them, update statuses in bulk,
and export everything to CSV.

54
00:03:18,496 --> 00:03:21,567
Open an application to see the candidate's
details,

55
00:03:21,567 --> 00:03:24,397
download the resume, and read the cover
letter.

56
00:03:24,597 --> 00:03:28,728
Use the Current Status dropdown to move them
through your hiring process.

57
00:03:29,408 --> 00:03:34,797
Every time the status changes, the candidate
is notified by email automatically.

58
00:03:35,477 --> 00:03:37,880
The same happens when you shortlist someone.

59
00:03:38,080 --> 00:03:41,116
And every change is recorded in the activity
log,

60
00:03:41,116 --> 00:03:43,533
with the time and the user who made it.

61
00:03:44,213 --> 00:03:49,282
You can also review every email the plugin has
sent under Settings, Email Logs.

62
00:03:49,962 --> 00:03:54,241
General Settings lets you set a global third-
party form shortcode,

63
00:03:54,241 --> 00:03:59,362
the number of jobs per page, the application
statuses, and the currency symbol.

64
00:04:00,042 --> 00:04:03,895
You can also show the application form for one
specific job.

65
00:04:04,095 --> 00:04:08,103
Add the [talentora_application_form] shortcode
with a job ID,

66
00:04:08,103 --> 00:04:10,402
and the form is linked to that job.

67
00:04:11,082 --> 00:04:15,502
For more details, including the user guide and
the developer docs,

68
00:04:15,502 --> 00:04:18,114
check the plugin page on WordPress.org.

69
00:04:18,314 --> 00:04:20,695
Thanks for watching, and happy hiring!

